# open62541-qnx change: tcp-peer-name
# SPDX-License-Identifier: MPL-2.0
#
# title: Pass the real address length to getnameinfo() for a new connection
# file: open62541.c
# upstream: arch/eventloop_posix_tcp.c
# test: core.connect.ipv4
#
# For the log line of a new connection the code calls getnameinfo() with the
# size of struct sockaddr_storage instead of the length that accept() has
# returned. A getnameinfo() that compares the length with the address family
# refuses that (the KAME code of FreeBSD 11 and older and of NetBSD 6 does;
# FreeBSD 12 and later accept a longer length). The host string is then used
# without having been set. o6q_envprobe shows what the target does
# (getnameinfo.storage_length); core.connect.ipv4 counts the getnameinfo
# warnings of the server.
#
@@ hunk
